    {
      "id": "912020d3-2949-450b-9d11-7d1b38d7aee3",
      "body": "\u4ee5\u4e0b\u306e\u6307\u793a\u3092\u57fa\u306b\u3001\u4e26\u5217\u8a08\u7b97\u53ef\u80fd\u306a\u30a2\u30d7\u30ea\u30b1\u30fc\u30b7\u30e7\u30f3\u3092\u5b9f\u88c5\u3057\u3088\u3046\u3068\u8003\u3048\u3066\u3044\u307e\u3059\u3002CG\u5206\u91ce\u306e\u7814\u7a76\u5ba4\u306b\u6240\u5c5e\u3057\u3066\u3044\u308b\u306e\u3067\u3001CG\u95a2\u9023\u306e\u30a2\u30d7\u30ea\u30b1\u30fc\u30b7\u30e7\u30f3\u3092\u4f5c\u308d\u3046\u3068\u3057\u3066\u3044\u307e\u3059\u3002\u7d20\u6734\u306b\u306f\u30ec\u30a4\u30c8\u30ec\u30fc\u30b7\u30f3\u30b0\u30fb\u30d1\u30b9\u30c8\u30ec\u30fc\u30b7\u30f3\u30b0\u304b\u306a\u3068\u601d\u3044\u307e\u3059\u304c\u3001\u6848\u3092\u6319\u3052\u3066\u304f\u3060\u3055\u3044\u3002\n\nYou are instead expected to find an interesting/realistic problem with which you can learn how parallel processing are applied to real problems\n\nSuch problems might require too much work to code from scratch by yourself; you are therefore free to take advantage of AI for it rather than finish a tiny example by yourself\n\nYou have to build and run the code by yourself on Miyabi\n\nThe execution time should be easily configured with command line parameters or compile time macros (e.g., -DX=1024), so that the serial baseline code finishes in a reasonable amount of time (e.g., a few minutes) and should be scaled for parallel execution later\n\nIt should produce some meaningful and verifiable results (results you can at least informally confirm correctness of)\n\nObviously, you also have to make sure that the problem has ample parallelism (solvable in parallel); exact speed up can be unknown at this point, of course, but you cannot choose an aribrary problem without any idea how to speed it up with parallel execution\n\nAbove considerations may force you to change the problem setting or goals along the way; be prepared for it and start early\n\nFor example, you obviously cannot finish an LLM pre-training with billion parameters that can speak fluent English within a few minutes\n\nInstead of immediately giving up LLM, consider lowering your goal to, for example, an LLM with much smaller vocaburary and much less ambitious goal regarding smartness; you don't have to abandon LLM\n\nThis kind of exploration is what you are supposed to spend time on in this exercise",
