              "output": "<path>/home/u26136/miyabi/notebooks/pd/pd02_app/code/problem.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: \n2: * _this is an example file you should finish_\n3: * write problem description, how the algorithm/baseline code works, and where you think you can apply parallel computing\n4: * if you are looking at this file from Jupyter, you can see the preview by right-clicking on the cell and \"Show Markdown Preview\"\n5: \n6: # Making XXXXXX from scratch\n7: \n8: # Problem\n9: \n10: [remove this] \n11: \n12: $$ s = \\sum_{n=0}^{\\infty} \\frac{1}{n^2} $$\n13: \n14: # How the algorithm/baseline code works\n15: \n16: ```\n17: double s = 0.0;\n18: for (n = 1000000; n >= 1; n--) {\n19:   s += 1 / ((double)n * (double)n);\n20: }\n21: ```\n22: \n23: # Where is parallelism\n24: \n25: - all $1/n^2$ tems can be done in parallel\n\n(End of file - total 25 lines)\n</content>",
              "metadata": {
                "preview": "\n* _this is an example file you should finish_\n* write problem description, how the algorithm/baseline code works, and where you think you can apply parallel computing\n* if you are looking at this file from Jupyter, you can see the preview by right-clicking on the cell and \"Show Markdown Preview\"\n\n# Making XXXXXX from scratch\n\n# Problem\n\n[remove this] \n\n$$ s = \\sum_{n=0}^{\\infty} \\frac{1}{n^2} $$\n\n# How the algorithm/baseline code works\n\n```\ndouble s = 0.0;\nfor (n = 1000000; n >= 1; n--) {\n  s += 1 / ((double)n * (double)n);\n}",
                "truncated": false,
